condensed|shortened|ADJECTIVE|made shorter while keeping main points|Reduced to a shorter form while retaining the main information.|được cô đọng; được rút gọn|The editor prepared a condensed account of the meeting.|Biên tập viên chuẩn bị một bản tường thuật cô đọng về cuộc họp.|Before a noun or after a linking verb; this sense concerns shortened information rather than condensed milk.|-
fashion|popular-style|NOUN|style currently popular|A style of clothes, appearance, or behaviour that is popular at a particular time.|thời trang; phong cách đang thịnh hành|Wide trousers have come back into fashion at the local college.|Quần ống rộng lại trở thành mốt tại trường cao đẳng địa phương.|Often uncountable in phrases such as in fashion and out of fashion.|0
fashion|manner|NOUN|way of doing something|A particular way in which something is done or happens.|cách; kiểu|She arranged the photographs in an unusual fashion.|Cô ấy sắp xếp những bức ảnh theo một cách khác thường.|Usually in a particular fashion, with an adjective describing the manner; separate from clothing style.|1
long-time|long-standing|ADJECTIVE|having lasted many years|Having continued in a role or relationship for a long period.|lâu năm|A long-time neighbour offered to look after the house.|Một người hàng xóm lâu năm đề nghị trông nom ngôi nhà.|Attributive adjective before a noun; compare the phrase for a long time, which describes duration.|0
prepare|make-ready|VERB|make ready for use or an event|To make someone or something ready for a purpose or coming event.|chuẩn bị|The volunteers prepared the room for the evening class.|Các tình nguyện viên chuẩn bị căn phòng cho lớp học buổi tối.|Transitive prepare something for; intransitive prepare for an event and prepare to do something are also used.|0
suffer|experience-distress|VERB|experience pain or difficulty|To experience physical pain, mental distress, or serious difficulty.|chịu đau đớn; chịu đựng|Many residents suffered from the noise during the night work.|Nhiều cư dân phải chịu đựng tiếng ồn trong thời gian thi công ban đêm.|Suffer from names a source of distress; suffer pain or hardship uses a direct object.|0
suffer|be-damaged|VERB|become worse through harm|To be harmed or become worse because of an adverse situation.|bị tổn hại; bị ảnh hưởng xấu|The garden suffered during the long dry spell.|Khu vườn bị ảnh hưởng xấu trong đợt khô hạn kéo dài.|Intransitive in this sense; the subject can be a place, activity, or quality rather than a person feeling pain.|1
